    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d13">

                <pb facs="0141" n="23" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg23"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr.
                            Lawton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-03-22"><hi rendition="#italic">March 22,
                        1889.</hi></date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 84.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your dispatch (No. 121) of
                    the 2d instant, with which you inclose copies of correspondence with the
                    ministry of foreign affairs relative to the expulsion from Austria of one Hugo
                    Klamer, a naturalized citizen of the United States.</p>
                <p>Your presentation of the case appears to have been discreet and proper, and is
                    accordingly approved. You will continue with the same due discretion to look
                    after the case and see that any rights to which Mr. Klamer may be entitled by
                    treaty or by the law of nations are not infringed without due appeal for his
                    protection.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
